WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.190 --> 00:00:04.490
Too Many Crooks. A dice negotiation game where your score

2
00:00:04.510 --> 00:00:07.110
depends on the dice other players decide to send you.

3
00:00:07.790 --> 00:00:11.190
Every die is a crook. Its number says which kind.

4
00:00:11.420 --> 00:00:15.940
A job needs a crew, one of each kind. You score their total.

5
00:00:16.370 --> 00:00:19.060
The catch: you send four dice to your rivals.

6
00:00:19.080 --> 00:00:21.260
Your crew is whatever they send you.

7
00:00:21.400 --> 00:00:24.860
And their pay? Whatever dice you have left over.

8
00:00:25.250 --> 00:00:28.670
Deals are out loud. Ruby, if you give me your six,

9
00:00:28.690 --> 00:00:32.460
I'll pay you six. She agrees and sends me her six.

10
00:00:32.700 --> 00:00:35.580
Moe makes her the same offer with two crooks.

11
00:00:35.970 --> 00:00:37.350
I send Ruby my six,

12
00:00:37.350 --> 00:00:39.640
and keep four dice to pay my crew.

13
00:00:40.260 --> 00:00:43.960
My crew: six, four and one. Eleven points.

14
00:00:44.150 --> 00:00:48.400
Then everyone pays their crew in secret, with all the dice they kept.

15
00:00:48.780 --> 00:00:53.550
My plan was to backstab Ruby all along, so I assign her crook a wage of one,

16
00:00:53.570 --> 00:00:56.170
giving her only one point instead of six.

17
00:00:56.480 --> 00:01:01.120
At the reveal, Ruby pays me nine. Moe gets nothing:

18
00:01:01.140 --> 00:01:03.970
promises aren't binding, but everyone saw it.

19
00:01:04.420 --> 00:01:06.880
Three to six players, twenty to thirty minutes.

20
00:01:06.900 --> 00:01:09.460
Most points after three jobs wins.

21
00:01:09.750 --> 00:01:13.360
Too Many Crooks. Play it in your browser at darrendon.com,

22
00:01:13.380 --> 00:01:15.490
or email me for a prototype.

